<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jinheung of Silla</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">526–576</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jinheung was king of Silla from 540 to 576 and its greatest early conqueror. Allied with Baekje, he took the Han river valley from Goguryeo and then seized it from Baekje in 553, gaining access to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-sea">Yellow Sea</a>. He annexed Daegaya and the remaining Gaya states in 562, erected boundary steles recording his tours, and founded the hwarang youth corps.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>King <b>Jinheung</b> (r. 540–576) allied with Baekje to drive Goguryeo from the Han River valley in 551, then seized Baekje's share in 553, gaining access to the Yellow Sea and direct contact with China.</blockquote><a href="/empire/silla">Silla · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Silla established a province at Bisabeol in 555 and <b>King Jinheung</b> erected a stele there in 561 recording his tour and naming his officials, marking the area's full incorporation.</blockquote><a href="/state/bihwa-gaya">Bihwa Gaya</a></li><li><blockquote>Silla absorbed the states one by one: Geumgwan Gaya surrendered in 532 and Daegaya fell to <b>King Jinheung</b> in 562.</blockquote><a href="/state/gaya-confederacy">Gaya confederacy</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gyeongju">Gyeongju</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/south-korea">South Korea</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=35.85,129.22&amp;year=558" aria-label="Gyeongju on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7810 869 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Jinheung of Silla"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8260 1139h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8260 1139h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=35.85,129.22&amp;year=558">What was here in 558 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
